      "text": [
        "708 - وَ رَأَى عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ مَسْجِداً بِالْكُوفَةِ قَدْ شُرِّفَ قَالَ «كَأَنَّهُ بِيعَةٌ إِنَّ اَلْمَسَاجِدَ لاَ تُشَرَّفُ تُبْنَى جُمّاً."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.708 - Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) saw a mosque in Kufa that had been decorated or elevated and said:\n\"It is as if it is a church. Mosques are not to be adorned; they should be built plain (simple).\""
        ]
      }
